  "worked_solution": "First, we calculate $v(t)$ by differentiating $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{4}-{t}^{2}+3t) \\\\  & =8{t}^{3}-2t+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $v(t)$ to find $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(8{t}^{3}-2t+3) \\\\  & =24{t}^{2}-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the acceleration at time $t=\\frac{1}{2}$ second, we substitute $t=\\frac{1}{2}$ into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(\\frac{1}{2}) & =24{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}-2 \\\\  & =24\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}-2 \\\\  & =4\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
